{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/819196-that-moment-when","id":819196,"title":"That moment when...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-29T06:59:10-08:00","id":819196,"title":"That moment when...","content":"Players do the unthinkable or go off on a tangent that was unexpected.<br /> <br /> We've probably all had them. The ones that spring to mind for me is the pack on the hunt for a deadly bsd pack and the Red Talon decides to forget that and start killing humans in the city while the rest of pack look on in horror and shock.<br /> <br /> The pack trying to get permission to enter a silver Fang sept and are put through tests of honor and loyalty upon being met to be allowed entrance to the sacred caern and the Fianna pulls a silver Klaive on the guardian and challenges them.<br /> <br /> The Bonegnawer who pushes his own pack mate that just healed him into the path of Thrall Frenzying foe rather than push him out of the way to keep it away from him.<br /> <br /> But my current mind boggling moment. The pack are looking into prophecies of the Apocalypse. They each get a prophecy. The metis gets one of an important perfect metis cub being born to two metis parents. The pack decide to investigate. They find the parents bodies bloodied and tattered and track the wyrm taint and blood and after some time tracking BSDs Banes and all sorts of bad end up face to face with Eeyarlagh Twice-Born holding the newborn child of destiny. Just Eeyarlagh and them. A pack of hardened garou.<br /> <br /> They decide dealing with the cub is above their pay grade (Fosterns, some with enough renown for Adren), and not knowing what to do with the baby they decide to let Eeyarlagh go with the child. Not that they, gaian garou who've spent over a year battling bsds, who've seen and been tortured by the evils of that tribe, who know through portents and visions that the child is important. Not that anyone garou of higher rank or importance at any of the other 4 caerns they've recently been involved with, nor they themselves were good enough or a better choice than this fanatic bsd. Nope. They even wished her good luck.<br /> <br /> I really did not see that coming.<br /> <br /> anyone else have any remembered moments? Or think the pack above should just be outright torn to shreds for giving an orphaned baby garou, destined to be of importance shared via visions from gaia, from a mysterious birth from between two sterile mules, that arrived as the red star in the sky first peaked through the umbral night skies over to an agent to the Wyrm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T09:33:17-08:00","id":819324,"title":"","content":"I... uh... wow. Knowingly causing harm to a fellow packmate in battle? That 'gnawer's ass would be grass in my game. Frenzying in the heat of combat and coming to blows on accident is one thing, but actively putting your packmates in harm's way? That's a paddling.<br /> <br /> Abandoning a Garou child to a servant of the Wyrm is also a massive dereliction of duty. There are Ronin with more scruples than that. A significant honor and wisdom penalty for all involved would be quite appropriate.<br /> <br /> My pack's philodox and ahroun do a pretty good job keeping the rest of the group on track, although that same philodox did <i>bite</i> the head off a state senator who was consorting (unwittingly) with agents of the Wyrm. What followed was an interesting Veil cleanup operation, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:17:57-08:00","id":819350,"title":"","content":"Yeah.... I dont think they even know icly how to explain their decision. Twice. Yep, the whole pack just to make sure it was ok chased after the BSD and baby, had a chat about fate, prophesy and destiny and decided a second time that this was the best thing.<br /> <br /> bring on the Apocalypse. <br /> <br /> I will say my players are pretty good at avoiding veil breaches and not biting heads of senators though.<br /> <br /> Yeah the Bonegnawer player opted out of ever returning after his pack mate died from thralling badness. All the plsyers found it quite funny and took it in stride but ...nope.. he wasnt going to face any fall out for his pcs actions. Never mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T11:33:02-08:00","id":819390,"title":"","content":"We had a character like that in our LARP. She insisted on taking drugs from the BSD's rap evan, then frenzied and had to be subdued. When it came to actually taking out the Fallen Ones, she said she was too tired to help us. My <i>Get of Fenris</i> had to convince the <i>Child of Gaia</i> that she should be given the opportunity to be thrown bodily at the Wyrm and die honorably. When she failed to appear the next session, we informed the HST that if she ever showed up again, she was getting a bullet to the head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T12:02:23-08:00","id":819405,"title":"","content":"We dont deny the philodox the chance to judge or the master of challenge to oversee a direct challenge before the sept. So anyone double tapping or going outside protocol and heirarchy (no matter how justified it may seem) gets a shame paddling in our game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> probably just as bad as the guilty party. <br /> <br /> Looks like now everyone still involved will now have a punishment Rite added to their list of personal events now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T03:07:51-08:00","id":819743,"title":"","content":"Ahadi game, African Fera plus one young Fianna. Main quest finished, big moot to wrap it all up. Fianna interrupts the moot because he is feeling emo and thinks the best was to honor his fallen comrades is by boycotting the Opening Howl. Our way-too-nice Galliard talks everybody down. The very next day, under a bright sunny sky in a green meadow, the moping Fianna manages to send the Galliard who saved him into a Frenzy, which somehow leads to the whole pack hacking the Fianna into bits. We storytellers just sat there horrified. &quot;Sunny day, green meadow&quot; have become winged words for our group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T06:27:58-08:00","id":819783,"title":"","content":"Sunny day, green meadow...when the Fianna fell.<br /> <br /> In the Tradition of garou story sharing I feel I should use this tale of warning in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T22:47:27-08:00","id":820182,"title":"","content":"Dear Gaia on a crutch, what in the Tellurian were these players/characters <i>thinking</i>? Refusing to rescue an innocent baby from the BSDs? A friggin' werewolf who's <i>too stoned to fight? </i>An emo Fianna who somehow gets so emo he <i>provokes his own pack into murdering him</i>?<br /> <br /> How do people come up with this stuff?<br /> <br /> And etherial, what does HST mean, anyway? I found several different meanings for HST on the Urban Dictionary, ranging from &quot;Horse Shit Tax&quot; to &quot;Hacker Standard Time&quot; to &quot;Hot Sluts with Tits and &quot;Human Sexual Thermos.&quot; Some clarification, please. (And please don't tell me that the rest of the pack had the hots for the fellow Garou female stoner, because y'know, violation of the First Tenet of the Litany, and all that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T03:33:11-08:00","id":820241,"title":"","content":"I'm not etherial. But I can answer the HST question.<br /> <br /> HST in RP usually means 'Head Story Teller' it's the one who oversees all the things where a group of STs may be necessary for a large group or setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T03:41:22-08:00","id":820242,"title":"","content":"As for how they come up with this stuff. I asked my group, on reflection even they have no idea why. They seem absolutely confused as to why they did that. <br /> <br /> From a point of observation it could be fear, uncertainty, that choice to turn a blind eye rather than make a bad decision and be held accountable later because it wasn't the right choice or handled perfectly. Leave it someone else now and if its a problem later we'll sort it out later once someone ekse tells us how and is willing to be at the other end of the finger point if it goes wrong. Maybe? I dont know. Wasn't in their brains at the time.<br /> <br /> Why be ok to icly take drugs and then not fight? Maybe being the centre of attention and perhaps being free or directed to act destructively with a clause of 'it wasnt me, the drugs made me do it' was perhaps more enjoyable than the risk of the character being in actual danger of death against the enemy in battle. I've certainly seen more characters willing to start something with allies on an even power level of themselves than take on the unknown power levels of the enemy. Maybe? I dont know, I dont play like that.<br /> <br /> why get yourself killed by others of your Sept? Again I dont know. Perhaps unhappiness with the character or the game? Maybe the fact they were thewolf among the fera and the closest reminder of atrocities of the garou against the other changers and decided 'if I get you to kill me then you're no better and I've proved it.' Who knows, maybe? Not my bag, I'd rather get involved in the story and be known for something great and valorous than getting everyone else to kill my pc.<br /> <br /> It could be suggested that sometimes a game is seen as a personal place that must revolve around that individual and what they, the PC and player want over the story itself. If it doesn't, then they do what they can to distance the plot they are not interested in or try to create a side plot just for them.<br /> <br /> But who'd admit to that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and I cant be sure that's why. <br /> <br /> It's a good question though and perhaps watching to see how they roll with the repercussions and in game demands that follow is a good way to determine whether it was an innocent slip of the mind, or something else.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, experiences, more WTF moments anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:36:35-08:00","id":820425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/819196-that-moment-when?p=819405#post819405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We dont deny the philodox the chance to judge or the master of challenge to oversee a direct challenge before the sept. So anyone double tapping or going outside protocol and heirarchy (no matter how justified it may seem) gets a shame paddling in our game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> probably just as bad as the guilty party.<br /> <br /> Looks like now everyone still involved will now have a punishment Rite added to their list of personal events now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, our Master of the Challenger was all for killing her, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T04:31:05-08:00","id":820879,"title":"","content":"That's certainly one way of speeding up the process and avoiding all the paperwork. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T01:33:56-08:00","id":821495,"title":"","content":"I remember a time when the Red Talon was stuck in the city and wanted to get the hell out, NOW. So he decides he wants to Step Sideways, and realises that he is going to have a hard time crossing the city Gauntlet and wants to help himself with a reflective surface. So he pees on the floor, looks into the puddle and proceeds to botch the roll and get stuck in the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T12:52:12-08:00","id":821827,"title":"","content":"I had that same goofy Philodox in my game kill a Black Spiral Dancer kinfolk wolf with a hatchet, and then proceed to attack another BSD kinfok (a human) while wielding the slain wolf. The Garou knocked the guy down and then pinned him, eventually smothering the guy to death with the wolf's corpse.<br /> <br /> The Philodox was basically forced to sit out the rest of the fight in order to pull this stunt. It took forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T03:05:02-08:00","id":822232,"title":"","content":"Pack go on a quest for a Path Stone to create a Caern for a Sept. They succeed. Deside they are bored so go looking for a fight with a group of Banes and BSDs to spice up the tale of their victory.<br /> <br /> a few botched combat rolls later and the pack are running for their lives. The Ahroun leader gives the Path Stone to the Ragabash and tells them to run back to the Sept with it, he will stay and hold off the malfean horde for the pack.<br /> <br /> The Ragabash decides he doesnt want the wyrm creatures following him either so &quot;wisely and with honor to rescue the rest of the pack I show the wyrm beasts the path stone and throw it over the moon path we are travelling. Do they follow after it?&quot; Yes. Yes they did. The pack made it safe back to the sept.The wyrm on the other hand got a shiny new path stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:13:42-08:00","id":822742,"title":"","content":"Kitsune gets tasked by the group with entering an enemy barrack through the Umbra, light it on fire, and get promptly out again. ST literally warns him that he needs to be very careful - it wasn't a very safe idea to begin with, the place is full of armed enemies, sleeping and awake, and the Kitsune does not have regeneration. Also he is a Metis and would cause a huge veil breach if he got overwhelmed. The fox gets in and takes long enough to lose the rest of the group completely, who have their own problems outside. It takes long enough to justify a 1 on 1 with the player. While he has the spotlight, he notices the two guards in the doorframe and ponders that he could take them out. ST asks him if he really really wants to try. Yes, he does. Gets incapacitated immediately, no fire, instead three months torture at the hands of evil scientists.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Also: Player in a crossover friendly game needs a new character, after he asked the ST to chop off his old character's head for plot/drama reasons. He then creates a Hunter. Pretty much introduces himself to the shifters as: &quot;Lol, that's funny, I'm a werewolf hunter. Let's be friends.&quot; Turns his back, gets immediately murdered and thrown into a dumpster, then lit on fire.<br /> Same player decides to play it safe and makes a Shadow Lord the next game. Manages to find the one area the ST set up as a trap for the whole pack, alone. Opens the door to find 5-ish people cocking shotguns and taking aim at him. He decides to get a good look at the situation before reacting. He gets the good look, also 5-ish shotgun blasts to the chest. Dead immediately.<br /> Same player then decides to play it super safe and make a Gurahl. That one lasted for 2 years, until he entered a &quot;boss fight&quot; without changing out of bear form, which also got him murdered. We were fighting vampires and could have had a flamethrower. Who advised against bringing the damn thing, because of the risk of it exploding? That player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","user":"Taci","date":". 02-03-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T00:56:22-08:00","id":823144,"title":"","content":"I had a player once, thinking of him makes me laugh but then i was pissed. He made Silver Fang character with his corporation!, max resources and contacts everywhere, he wished to patrol the city like Batman, he even wanted his own signal. WTF i though and stoped the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T02:38:48-08:00","id":823185,"title":"","content":"Had a guy playing a bonegnawer who shot himself in the head to prove to the totem Ares that he was willing to die for the cause...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T08:08:33-08:00","id":823355,"title":"","content":"These are so good we should rename this thread something like the Rusted Record and fill it with all these epic tales of failure and what-the-fuckery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8365-pensman","name":"Pensman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8365_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T08:15:27-08:00","id":823362,"title":"","content":"Most of my players for whatever reason at least in Werewolf do not do anything this bad. That said a few wtf were they thinking moments have occurred at my table over the 20 years that I've run WtA games:<br /> Suffer the Children this is the chronicle name. A bit of background this chronicle started as a one off story that morphed into a three-year chronicle. The events here happened early in the chronicle Chapter 2. The characters have successfully infiltrated a boarding school that is home to a slaving ring and churns out a large number of Formori. The pack led by the intrepid Red Talon Philodox begins the full out assault on the staff. They quickly overcome the teachers except for the headmistress who retreats to the basement. The pack charges after her the true master a specially designed bane is materializing. This bane causes terror one player the second on the narrow winding staircase for whatever reason decides on his action to run away. Knocking every player behind him to the concrete floor below. The Silver Fang theurge spend his action to heal the Ahroun. The theurge is the target of the band's attack. He is dead. The character that ran away is forced by the remaining pack members to run a gauntlet. The player to this day insists that he was only acting in character.<br /> <br /> Suffer the Children chapter 6 or 7 same player same character decides to ignore the Red Talon Philodox that wanted the Bone Gnawer Metis Ahroun and Uktena Ragabash to stay hidden while the rest of the pack investigated the neighboring town. The player convinces the other that staying hidden means going to the local diner is what the rest of the pack meant. The entire town turns out for the welcome to Garou party. This time the character does not survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T03:52:35-08:00","id":824156,"title":"","content":"In game update<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/819196-that-moment-when#post819196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my current mind boggling moment. The pack are looking into prophecies of the Apocalypse. They each get a prophecy. The metis gets one of an important perfect metis cub being born to two metis parents. The pack decide to investigate. They find the parents bodies bloodied and tattered and track the wyrm taint and blood and after some time tracking BSDs Banes and all sorts of bad end up face to face with Eeyarlagh Twice-Born*holding the newborn child of destiny. Just Eeyarlagh and them. A pack of hardened garou.<br /> <br /> They decide dealing with the cub is above their pay grade (Fosterns, some with enough renown for Adren), and not knowing what to do with the baby they decide to let Eeyarlagh go with the child. Not that they, gaian garou who've spent over a year battling bsds, who've seen and been tortured by the evils of that tribe, who know through portents and visions that the child is important. Not that anyone garou of higher rank or importance at any of the other 4 caerns they've recently been involved with, nor they themselves were good enough or a better choice than this fanatic bsd. Nope. They even wished her good luck.<br /> <br /> I really did not see that coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upon realising their mistake icly, the group had the choice to either go back home and face the music, make a run for it or try and do something to salvage it. They decided to try and salvage it first before going back. It didn't happen. Basically half the pack decided to bravely hide in the shadows of BSD Hive, while sending the Metis in to look around, another wondered off looking for something else. They ended up running away, rather than risk dying.<br /> <br /> So back to the Sept they went after another pack (NPCs) came to collect them.<br /> <br /> We held a moot judgement of the situation, each character getting a chance to speak on their own behalf of the events and the troubling prophecies or as a pack. It didn't go great, the Child of Gaia blamed it on Gaia lol, but ultimately said it was failure as a theurge and his own perceptions that led him to give his alpha bad advice. The Galliard Alpha blamed it on everyone giving him poor advice but then asked the philodox of the Sept only punish him as he was the leader, The Ahroun didn't like the idea of someone else trying to take the blame for his shame..although he did get his own Deedname wrong when introducing himself before the council and the Philodox wouldn't give any judgement on the situation or define what went wrong and why.<br /> <br /> So, Rites of Punishment, losing of renown and sept positions, and a loss of Rank. Satired and to be ignored for three months and not allowed to leave the Sept. The Septs Ragabash gave them all new Deednames of Shame and I quickly relayed what happens on Sept for the next three months and unveiled some of the repercussions of their actions visible across the worlds as time passed.<br /> <br /> Overall, it actually went really well. The Troupe really played this out fantastically and are already looking at new ways to define their characters and their next steps as a pack with the lessons learned. Despite the &quot;what in the name of Gaia is going on?&quot;-ness of it all, this turned out to be an amazingly emotionally charged, humbling and re-defining moment for players and characters alike. So impressed how much of it was taken in stride and utilised not for the failure but for the story they continue to tell. Completely worth helping to the Apocalypse take another step forwards <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}